# torch and the ONNX runtime for a build with no GPU.
#
# The CPU index matters as much as the CUDA one: the default PyPI torch
# wheel carries the CUDA runtime, which is most of a gigabyte that a CPU
# build has no use for.
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu

-r base.in

torch==2.12.1
# torchvision pins torch to an exact version, so the two move together and
# both are named here. Left undeclared it arrives through `timm` and
# `ultralytics` as a bare requirement, and the resolver silently picks
# whichever build happens to pin the torch above -- which is how this lock
# sat on an older torchvision than the index offered.
torchvision==0.27.1
# onnxruntime 1.23.2 ships wheels for cp310 through cp313 only, so resolving
# it under 3.14 fails with "No matching distribution found" -- the
# requires_python metadata says >=3.10 and gives no hint, the ABI tags are
# what run out. 1.24.1 is the first release carrying cp314, and it drops
# cp310, which VIAME still offers. So pin per interpreter rather than moving
# every build onto a new runtime. Upstream f21a0ac1b, as a marker rather
# than a CMake branch.
onnxruntime==1.23.2 ; python_version < "3.14"
onnxruntime==1.24.1 ; python_version >= "3.14"
